==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|non}} {{recons|sitjaną|lang=gem-pro}}, akin to Old English {{term|sittan|lang=ang}}, Old Saxon {{term|sittian|lang=osx}}, Old Frisian {{term|sitta|lang=ofs}}, Old High German {{term|sizzen|lang=goh}}, Gothic {{term|𐍃𐌹𐍄𐌰𐌽|tr=sitan|lang=got}}. Ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|non}} {{recons|sed-||sit|lang=ine-pro}}.

===Verb===
'''sitja''' (''strong class V:'' [[sat]] – [[sátu]] - [[setinn]])

# to [[sit]]

